{"name":"Ancestral","hex":"#d0c1c3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ancestral","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, pertaining to, derived from, or possessed by, an ancestor or ancestors."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An ancestor or forbear.","A descendant of one's ancestors."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ancestral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Ancestor","blocks":[{"text":"In genealogy and evolutionary biology, an ancestor, also known as a forefather, fore-elder, or a forebear, is a parent or (recursively) the parent of an antecedent. Ancestor is \"any person from whom one is descended. In law, the person from whom an estate has been inherited.\""}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ancestor","wikidata":"Q402152"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"ancestral":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ea/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-ancestral.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ea/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-ancestral.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-ancestral.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/e/ea/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-ancestral.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-ancestral.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.53},{"title":"Confucius Temple @ Foshan Ancestral Temple 09","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/91/Confucius_Temple_%40_Foshan_Ancestral_Temple_09.jpg/500px-Confucius_Temple_%40_Foshan_Ancestral_Temple_09.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Confuci